    skos:closeMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23012379> ;
    skos:definition "an esculent (*Apium graveolens*), the blanched footstalks of the leaves are eaten in England, and in many countries the leaves and seeds are used for soup. The seeds are also employed as a stimulant by the native medical practitioners of India. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 90]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_celery" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Celery"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0085 (Vegetables Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 90."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
